{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "55ea9e5e-27bd-59aa-91a1-12002a8e8a34",
    "name": "Crop Sown Registry Dashboard Service",
    "description": "Read-only aggregate API of the crop sown registry, used by the OAN dashboards.\n\n- Every chart: `GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/charts/<chartId>` returns a JSON array of rows.\n- Filters (all optional, combined with AND) are included on each request but disabled; enable the ones you need. `all` or omitted means no filter.\n  - `region`, `zone`, `woreda`, `kebele`: P-codes, in any of the forms `ET04`, `region-ET04`, `REGION_ET04`.\n  - `recordState`: record status, case-insensitive. Without it, only ACTIVE records are counted (except `cropByRecordState`).\n  - `status`: approval-workflow status (`APPROVAL_STATUS_APPROVED` or `APPROVED`).\n  - `season`: production season (`CROP_SEASON_MEHER` or `MEHER`).\n  - `cropYear`: crop year, e.g. `2026`.\n  - `commodity`: crop lookup key (`CROP_COMMODITY_WHEAT`), its last part (`WHEAT`) or the label.\n- Areas are hectares.\n- The collection-level test checks status 200 and the exact response keys per chart. Example responses come from the service test fixture.\n\nSet `baseUrl` (collection variable, or the environment) to the service URL. The service has no authentication and is meant to be reachable on the private network only.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
